<h1>Altamont Pass Wind Farm</h1>
<p>I chose the Altamont Pass Wind Farm in California. It is one of the oldest and largest wind energy areas in the United States. The wind turbines produce renewable electricity, linking them to climate change solutions and green technology. Still, they are also a major issue, as they are among the leading causes of bird deaths. 
Located within Northern California in the Altamont Pass of the Diablo Range, it covers large dry hills and grassland landscapes. Known to be one of the earliest wind farms, built in the early 1980s. It produces around 125 MW on average and 1.1 terawatt-hours (TWh) yearly.
