<p>Unfortunately, although wind farms provide benefits like renewable energy and reduce the need for fossil fuels, animals like golden eagles and hawks are at risk of being killed by colliding with the rotating blades. Golden eagles are federally protected birds, and in the year 2007 alone, 70 eagles were killed among the 1300 bird casualties, with a total of 4700 bird deaths annually.</p>

